ceb38ae4b5ebe8e388d9a894b5a5214345c09627e8acc00e2c10796e07410","event_uuid":"52e6aede-df37-40b2-8cb5-88d26db96b6b","position":{"commit_sha":"0f1bffff3ea5312c9fcc7cb5973b143aa83cef68","position":"1787622299589832001-52e6aede-df37-40b2-8cb5-88d26db96b6b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"94bcd2414f9c5e862385aa723fa65213faf46b03ae033c6936edd628246fddfd","event_uuid":"0ceeb896-da4b-4802-8350-d72655c24869","position":{"commit_sha":"eee01110b26017e7fca8fee2613d7828a7dc749d","position":"1787622322664761001-0ceeb896-da4b-4802-8350-d72655c24869"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787594440498360001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"2cff0724-850a-4133-9d76-951df4aa9017","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"a45f-bd45-513a-49cb"},{"link_uuid":"300ec9ce-dc6d-498b-b390-7e4cac47e7f3","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7886-f365-5884-47e4"},{"link_uuid":"f9335b1a-14d2-464c-b658-e338dabb3ee2","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9297-5ea0-0a32-4040"},{"link_uuid":"cdb770ea-8850-4e70-97db-4531bd53cfe7","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4b09-9af9-9f42-4a08"}],"description":"Add the self-contained rebar MCP HTTP service to the box per ADR deft-evolutive-mosasaur: a new\n`mcp` compose service + `Dockerfile.mcp` running loopback-published `rebar-mcp` HTTP, and an nginx\n`/mcp/` TLS-edge location with a switchable upstream so the autodeploy slice\n(panicky-sylphish-foxterrier) can flip blue→green atomically. INFRA + the `/health` code only; the\nlive AWS deploy is approval-gated (a human performs it). Autodeploy logic lives in foxterrier,\nsecrets in avians.\n\n## Scope\n- `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml`: an `mcp` service (built from `Dockerfile.mcp`),\n  loopback-published `127.0.0.1:8091` (Gerrit 8080, review-bot REVIEW_BOT_PORT, opcert 8090),\n  `restart: always`, a `healthcheck` hitting `/health`, and `stop_grace_period: 1260s` (covers the\n  1200s app SIGTERM grace + margin so Docker never SIGKILLs mid-op). Fail-closed HTTP posture via\n  env: `REBAR_MCP_TRANSPORT=http`, `REBAR_MCP_HTTP_HOST=0.0.0.0`, `REBAR_MCP_HTTP_PORT=8091`,\n  `REBAR_MCP_HTTP_TLS_AT_EDGE=true`, `REBAR_MCP_HTTP_ALLOWED_HOSTS`/`REBAR_MCP_HTTP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS`\n  (external host/origin), `REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ENABLED=1`, `REBAR_MCP_AUTH_STRATEGIES=static`,\n  `REBAR_MCP_AUTH_RESOURCE_SERVER_URL`, `REBAR_MCP_AUTH_STATIC_TOKENS_FILE`. `MCP_PATHS` for the\n  autodeploy change-detector is declared as a compose comment so foxterrier can consume it.\n- `infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp` (NEW): builds `rebar-mcp` from the same repo-root context +\n  committed `uv.lock` as `Dockerfile.opcert` (`python:3.12-slim`,\n  `uv sync --locked --no-dev --extra agents --extra mcp`). CMD boots `rebar-mcp` (http via env). A\n  container `HEALTHCHECK` curls loopback `/health`.\n- `infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template`: a new `location /mcp/` proxying to a named `upstream rebar_mcp`\n  whose `server` line is the materialized include `include /etc/nginx/mcp-upstream*.conf;` (the\n  flip seam). TLS terminates at nginx (mirrors `/review/` + `/opcert/`).\n- `infra/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf` (NEW, committed seed): `server 127.0.0.1:8091;`.\n- `infra/scripts/materialize-mcp-upstream.sh` (NEW): the concrete committed fresh-boot installer —\n  copies the committed seed to `/etc/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf` ONLY IF absent (so a foxterrier flip\n  is never clobbered on redeploy), then `nginx -s reload`. Local-file seed (no SSM); idempotent.\n- `infra/scripts/compose-up.sh`: call `materialize-mcp-upstream.sh` before `docker compose up`,\n  beside the existing `materialize-opcert-guard.sh` call, same non-fatal WARN pattern.\n- `/health` on the MCP server exposing an integer `in_flight` gauge counting ONLY certified ops\n  (review_plan/verify_completion/review_code/scan_spec), plus a bounded SIGTERM grace so a retiring\n  container lets an in-flight op finish. The gauge feeds foxterrier's retire check; it does not gate\n  the deploy. New health/gauge/signal code lives in a NEW module `src/rebar/_mcp_health.py`\n  (mcp_server.py is at its 800-LOC cap), wired from `build_server`/`main`.\n\n## nginx switchable upstream — grounded fresh-boot + flip\nAn nginx `upstream {}` with ZERO `server` lines is a config error (`nginx -t`: \"no servers are\ninside upstream\") — unlike the `/opcert/` `map` whose `default 0` makes a zero-match glob safe. So:\n(1) the template GLOB-includes `mcp-upstream*.conf`; (2) this change ships the committed seed\n`infra/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf`; (3) the NEW committed installer `materialize-mcp-upstream.sh`,\nwired into `compose-up.sh`, copies that seed to `/etc/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf` (only-if-absent)\nbefore the stack comes up, so a fresh boot has exactly one backend and `nginx -t` passes.\nCorrection: NO committed script renders `rebar.conf.template` via `envsubst` today (it is only an\nexample comment in the template header); this plan relies only on the committed installer above.\nfoxterrier re-points blue→green by atomically rewriting that single file + `nginx -s reload`. The AC\nrenders the template WITH the seed present.\n\n## /health auth exemption\nCONFIRMED against installed `mcp` 1.29.0 (not from memory): `FastMCP.custom_route`'s own docstring\nstates \"Routes using this decorator will not require authorization\", and `streamable_http_app`\nappends `_custom_starlette_routes` as bare Starlette `Route`s while wrapping ONLY the mounted MCP\nendpoint in `RequireAuthMiddleware`. So under `REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ENABLED=1` an unauthenticated probe of\n`/health` returns 200; only `/mcp` enforces the `static` bearer. The in-process test asserts\n`/health`→200 with auth ENABLED and no token, so the exemption is proven executably.\n\n## SIGTERM grace (concrete numbers)\n`_mcp_health.py` defines `DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS = 1200` (a module constant, the\n`review_bot/config.py` budget precedent — not a rebar config key). On SIGTERM the process waits up\nto 1200s for `in_flight` to reach 0, then exits; compose `stop_grace_period: 1260s` covers it.\n\n## Approach\nMirror the proven opcert edge (loopback service + nginx location) but expose a switchable upstream\nrather than a hardcoded `proxy_pass host:port`, because the ADR's blue-green cutover re-points the\nupstream atomically. `/health` counts only expensive ops so retirement waits on billable work, not\ntrivial reads. Shared base image keeps build cost low; retained images bounded by the existing prune.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] In-process ASGI (docker NOT required): `/health` from the FastMCP `streamable_http_app`\n  returns JSON with an integer `in_flight`. Oracle: `in_flight` reads 0 at idle, increments while a\n  stubbed certified op is held in flight, returns to 0 after — via the real endpoint through a\n  Starlette TestClient; a trivial read does NOT move it (contrast). `/health` also returns 200\n  WITHOUT a bearer while `REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ENABLED=1` (auth-exemption oracle).\n- [x] Fail-closed boot: a non-loopback bind with NO TLS-at-edge/allowlist ack makes `build_server`\n  raise `McpStartupError` (ADR-0050 guard message); with the ack it boots. Oracle: the existing\n  `_resolve_http_runtime` gates, asserted directly.\n- [x] nginx `/mcp/` proxies to a named `upstream rebar_mcp` whose `server` line is the materialized\n  include `mcp-upstream*.conf`; the committed seed `infra/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf` supplies\n  `server 127.0.0.1:8091;`; and `materialize-mcp-upstream.sh` (called from `compose-up.sh`) installs\n  it only-if-absent. Oracle: structural parse of the rendered template + seed + installer wiring\n  (`nginx -t` when a binary is available).\n- [x] SIGTERM grace: with `in_flight` > 0 a SIGTERM does NOT exit immediately and exits 0 once the\n  gauge drains, within the 1200s bound — a subprocess/signal test driving the `_mcp_health` grace\n  handler; and `stop_grace_period` (1260s) ≥ `DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS` (1200s), asserted\n  structurally over compose + the module.\n\n## Testing\nStarlette TestClient over `streamable_http_app` for `/health` idle/inflight/contrast + auth\nexemption; direct `build_server` assertions for the fail-closed gates; structural parse of the nginx\ntemplate + seed + installer wiring; a subprocess/signal SIGTERM test; a numeric assertion tying\n`stop_grace_period` to `DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS`. No docker dependency.\n\n## File impact\n`infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp` (new), `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml`,\n`infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template`, `infra/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf` (new),\n`infra/scripts/materialize-mcp-upstream.sh` (new), `infra/scripts/compose-up.sh`,\n`src/rebar/_mcp_health.py` (new), `src/rebar/mcp_server.py`, tests under `tests/`.\n\n## Compat / rollback\nPurely additive — new service, new port, new nginx location. Rollback = remove the `mcp`\nservice/location + seed + installer call (gerrit/review-bot/opcert unaffected). Trust boundary: new\nauthenticated endpoint — `static` bearer at `/mcp` + TLS at the nginx edge; `/health` is\nintentionally unauthenticated (no secrets, only an integer gauge).\n\nDepends on: deft-evolutive-mosasaur (ADR). Blocks: panicky-sylphish-foxterrier, unmythical-uninspired-olm.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_health.py","reason":"NEW: in-flight gauge (certified ops only), /health route, bounded SIGTERM grace, http run helper"},{"path":"src/rebar/mcp_server.py","reason":"wire wire_health() in build_server; route main() through run_mcp() for the graceful http run"},{"path":"infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp","reason":"NEW: build rebar-mcp http image (uv --extra agents --extra mcp) + /health HEALTHCHECK"},{"path":"infra/compose/docker-compose.yml","reason":"add mcp service (loopback 8091, http posture env, healthcheck, stop_grace_period, MCP_PATHS)"},{"path":"infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template","reason":"add named upstream rebar_mcp (materialized glob include) + /mcp/ location"},{"path":"infra/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf","reason":"NEW: committed seed upstream target (127.0.0.1:8091) foxterrier re-points on flip"},{"path":"infra/scripts/materialize-mcp-upstream.sh","reason":"NEW: install seed to /etc/nginx only-if-absent + nginx reload"},{"path":"infra/scripts/compose-up.sh","reason":"wire materialize-mcp-upstream.sh call (non-fatal WARN) beside opcert guard"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py","reason":"tests: /health idle/inflight/contrast + auth-exempt + SIGTERM grace"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py","reason":"NEW: structural infra tests (Dockerfile.mcp, compose mcp service, nginx upstream/seed/installer)"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","a45f-bd45-513a-49cb"],["parent","jira-reb-3527"],["relates_to","4b09-9af9-9f42-4a08"],["relates_to","7886-f365-5884-47e4"],["relates_to","9297-5ea0-0a32-4040"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"jira-reb-3527","parent_status_uuid":"52e6aede-df37-40b2-8cb5-88d26db96b6b","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"fd4a-4e91-f179-4932","ticket_type":"story","title":"rebar-mcp HTTP transport service on the AWS box (compose + Dockerfile + nginx /mcp/ route)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b6515011-9e81-45b3-a01d-0707fc8b3349","1bbad667-2e96-41cd-afd9-852da624db47","53586f45-4cb7-42c1-b50b-f976fd0a8166","6e54c176-2ff7-4df9-b79a-2dde2d256839","d0143f85-84bf-4c3c-bfb7-e34ea3771d58","7c7aafa0-9fe2-4eed-9193-54d2bea1c1b6","ef32593c-c1ef-489a-a3aa-34f2e4f60531","300ec9ce-dc6d-498b-b390-7e4cac47e7f3","f9335b1a-14d2-464c-b658-e338dabb3ee2","cdb770ea-8850-4e70-97db-4531bd53cfe7","5953cad8-e5a8-4f39-96e7-062b7e5ffac3","0b225399-ff47-4855-a5af-6d335f408a5a","fd227dc5-274d-44fb-bb30-cf087f33dcb7","52e6aede-df37-40b2-8cb5-88d26db96b6b","0ceeb896-da4b-4802-8350-d72655c24869"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787626432422867001,"uuid":"198ee932-eac8-4386-b3f1-f7fdebd3e019"}